{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/7ud8ra9s","slide":1,"text":"Proof for AI-generated fixes.","textPreview":"Proof for AI-generated fixes.","textChars":29,"textLines":1,"bbox":[78,270,450,80]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/k7m9gvq1","slide":1,"text":"ADVERSARIAL PR VERIFICATION","textPreview":"ADVERSARIAL PR VERIFICATION","textChars":27,"textLines":1,"bbox":[80,580,410,28]}
{"kind":"image","id":"im/gzytg72x","slide":1,"name":"","alt":"A cobalt glass block intersected by a coral verification beam","bbox":[0,0,1280,720]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/czxh3e","slide":1,"text":"Open simply: AI coding agents can fix bugs, but they cannot prove the fix works. Popper is the gate that asks for proof.\n\n[Sources]\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/public/product-thumbnail.png — locally generated project thumbnail\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/README.md — product description"}
{"kind":"slide","id":"sl/hmkwye","slide":2,"title":"THE PROBLEM FOUND US FIRST","textShapes":8}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/rm9czul0","slide":2,"text":"THE PROBLEM FOUND US FIRST","textPreview":"THE PROBLEM FOUND US FIRST","textChars":26,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,52,600,28]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/snitszml","slide":2,"text":"We became the bottleneck.","textPreview":"We became the bottleneck.","textChars":25,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,98,940,72]}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/d8ru1436","slide":2,"bbox":[72,226,1136,0]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/e90bu94r","slide":2,"text":"BUILDER","textPreview":"BUILDER","textChars":7,"textLines":1,"bbox":[76,276,240,28]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/fa9c3ulc","slide":2,"text":"AI gave us fixes\nin minutes.","textPreview":"AI gave us fixes | in minutes.","textChars":28,"textLines":2,"bbox":[72,326,470,146]}
{"kind":"shape","id":"sh/0bitwzmh","slide":2,"bbox":[620,258,4,276]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/1cbu5432","slide":2,"text":"REVIEWER","textPreview":"REVIEWER","textChars":8,"textLines":1,"bbox":[690,276,240,28]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/mdkby94n","slide":2,"text":"We still had to prove\nevery one.","textPreview":"We still had to prove | every one.","textChars":32,"textLines":2,"bbox":[686,326,510,146]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/netc7el8","slide":2,"text":"The faster agents wrote, the more human trust became the scarce resource.","textPreview":"The faster agents wrote, the more human trust became the scarce resource.","textChars":73,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,570,1040,54]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/rap07m5w","slide":2,"text":"POPPER  ·  02","textPreview":"POPPER  ·  02","textChars":13,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,674,210,24]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/hmkwye","slide":2,"text":"Make the problem personal. We used AI agents to build faster, but every convincing patch left us accountable for the merge. Then generalize: every team adopting coding agents inherits this trust bottleneck.\n\n[Sources]\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/AGENTS.md — documented parallel AI-agent workflow\n- Team experience and narrative supplied by the project creators"}
