{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/utgz250z","slide":9,"text":"POPPER  ·  09","textPreview":"POPPER  ·  09","textChars":13,"textLines":1,"bbox":[72,674,210,24]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/4ar4ie","slide":9,"text":"These are the engineering lessons that made Popper trustworthy. We separate inconclusive tests, infrastructure failures, and model opinion. Missing evidence blocks instead of creating false confidence.\n\n[Sources]\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/docs/DECISIONS.md — evidence boundaries and fail-closed decisions\n- /Users/NithinAwasome/Downloads/Daytona-Hacksprint/docs/PROGRESS.md — implementation challenges and verification history"}
